From 4e3d6506fc3e62a343700a10570d5e6aff3bc030 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Fran=C3=A7ois=20Roux?= <info@humanlearning.ch>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:25:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] arm64: dts: qcom: sp12: camera subsystem, board fixes and
 EL2 audio attach

Builds the Surface Pro 12 device tree from the UPSTREAM DTS instead of the
vendor DTB we have been decompiling since June. Three sources, in this order:

  hamoa.dtsi, purwa.dtsi   the camera subsystem (cci0, cci1, camss, csiphy),
                           from Mias van Klei's series as carried by CyberMyth OS
  x1p42100-microsoft-sp12in.dts  the nine board patches from his Gentoo overlay:
                           volume GPIOs put back the right way round, backlight
                           regulators, DisplayPort audio, iris enabled, charge
                           limit through nvmem, phantom thermal sensor removed,
                           rfkill disabled, CMA reservation dropped
  remoteproc nodes         qcom,broken-reset, ours, for the EL2 attach path

Two conflicts with 7.3, both resolved as duplicates rather than by force:
a second /delete-node/ &iris_opp_table and a second camcc node, since upstream
gained both since their 7.2-rc7 base.

Verified before installing: zap-shader disabled and PCIe SMMU okay in the EL2
variant (slbounce's conditions), iris disabled at EL2 and enabled at EL1,
qcom,broken-reset on both remoteprocs, and the volume keys now on gpio6/gpio8.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
